PUBLIC RESPONSE: [H,8]

The ten letters have to be strictly increasing and the value that is written down is the digital-root of the alphabetic rank, i.e. dr(P)=P if P≤9 and dr(P)=s₁(P) if P>9.

Putting
dr(P1)=6 ⇒ P1∈{6,15,24}
dr(P2)=7 ⇒ P2∈{7,16,25}
dr(P4)=3 ⇒ P4∈{3,12,21}
dr(P5)=5 ⇒ P5∈{5,14,23}
dr(P6)=7 ⇒ P6∈{7,16,25}
dr(P7)=8 ⇒ P7∈{8,17,26}
dr(P8)=9 ⇒ P8∈{9,18}
dr(P9)=1 ⇒ P9∈{1,10,19}
dr(P10)=8⇒ P10∈{8,17,26}

with P1<P2<P3<P4<P5<P6<P7<P8<P9<P10 the only feasible
increasing chain in 1…26 is

P1=6=F , P2=7=G , P4=12=L , P5=14=N , P6=16=P , P7=17=Q ,
P8=18=R , P9=19=S , P10=26=Z

and P3 has to lie strictly between 7 and 12.  The first admissible
choice which keeps the three opening digital-roots consecutive is

P3=8 = H ,  dr(P3)=8

so that the written digital-roots are

6,7,8,3,5,7,8,9,1,8

i.e. F G H L N P Q R S Z in alphabetical order.  The missing
written value is 8 and it stands for the letter H.

